---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import CtaBanner from '../../components/CtaBanner.astro';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import auditLogImg from '../../assets/audit-log.png';
import clientPortalImg from '../../assets/client-portal.png';
---

<Layout
  title="Trust, Role Portals & Audit Trail — Brift"
  description="Every important action leaves a trace. 4 role portals (Owner, Site Manager, Architect, Client), immutable audit logs, and reversing entries."
>
  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="relative pt-16 pb-14 sm:pt-24 sm:pb-20 bg-bg border-b border-line overflow-hidden">
    <div class="hero-gradient-blob" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="relative mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 text-center space-y-4">
      <span class="inline-block text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-blue bg-blue-soft px-3.5 py-1 rounded-full">
        SECURITY & ACCOUNTABILITY
      </span>
      <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl lg:text-6xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-ink leading-tight">
        Every important action leaves a trace.
      </h1>
      <p class="text-lg sm:text-xl text-muted max-w-2xl mx-auto leading-relaxed">
        Nothing in Brift is quietly deleted or manipulated. Built specifically for construction owners who require complete accountability across all active projects.
      </p>
      <div class="pt-2">
        <a href="/book-a-demo" class="inline-flex items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-blue px-7 py-3.5 text-sm font-semibold text-white hover:bg-blue-hover transition-all shadow-sm">
          Book a Live Security Walkthrough
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 4 Role Portals Section -->
  <section class="py-16 sm:py-24 bg-white border-b border-line">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="text-center max-w-3xl mx-auto mb-16 space-y-3">
        <span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-blue bg-blue-soft px-3 py-1 rounded-full">
          ACCESS CONTROL
        </span>
        <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-ink">
          Give everyone the access they actually need
        </h2>
        <p class="text-base text-muted">
          One central database, four distinct viewports. Each role sees only what their responsibilities permit.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-6">
        <div class="rounded-card border border-line bg-bg p-6 space-y-3 reveal">
          <span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-blue bg-blue-soft px-2.5 py-1 rounded-full">
            ROLE 01
          </span>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink">Owner / Admin</h3>
          <ul class="space-y-2 text-xs text-muted leading-relaxed">
            <li>• Verifies money, bills, stock moves and stages</li>
            <li>• Sees every site, person, report and bank account</li>
            <li>• Assigns cash balances to site managers</li>
            <li>• Exports annual financials and debt ledgers</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-card border border-line bg-bg p-6 space-y-3 reveal delay-100">
          <span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-blue bg-blue-soft px-2.5 py-1 rounded-full">
            ROLE 02
          </span>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink">Site Manager</h3>
          <ul class="space-y-2 text-xs text-muted leading-relaxed">
            <li>• Records purchases & snaps bills on mobile</li>
            <li>• Marks worker attendance full or half day</li>
            <li>• Pays contractors from assigned cash funds</li>
            <li>• Works strictly within their assigned project sites</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-card border border-line bg-bg p-6 space-y-3 reveal delay-200">
          <span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-blue bg-blue-soft px-2.5 py-1 rounded-full">
            ROLE 03
          </span>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink">Architect</h3>
          <ul class="space-y-2 text-xs text-muted leading-relaxed">
            <li>• Uploads structural & architectural drawings</li>
            <li>• Manages document versions & drawing revisions</li>
            <li>• Raises material expense requests for approval</li>
            <li>• Reviews 10-stage checklist execution</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-card border border-line bg-bg p-6 space-y-3 reveal delay-300">
          <span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-blue bg-blue-soft px-2.5 py-1 rounded-full">
            ROLE 04
          </span>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink">Client Portal</h3>
          <ul class="space-y-2 text-xs text-muted leading-relaxed">
            <li>• Sees only their own project progress & spend</li>
            <li>• Records payment references for admin verification</li>
            <li>• Signs documents with digital e-signatures</li>
            <li>• Submits feedback & star ratings to admin</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Client Portal Screenshot Section -->
  <section class="py-16 sm:py-24 bg-bg border-b border-line">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-12 gap-12 items-center">
        <div class="lg:col-span-6 space-y-6 reveal">
          <span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-blue bg-blue-soft px-3 py-1 rounded-full">
            CLIENT TRANSPARENCY
          </span>
          <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-ink">
            A private portal for your clients
          </h2>
          <p class="text-base text-muted leading-relaxed">
            Build unshakeable client trust. Instead of sending messy spreadsheets over email, invite clients to their own portal where they track payments, download verified statements, and sign agreements digitally.
          </p>
          <ul class="space-y-2.5 text-sm text-ink-2">
            <li class="flex items-center gap-2">✓ Verified stage completion signoffs</li>
            <li class="flex items-center gap-2">✓ Direct feedback history with admin response</li>
            <li class="flex items-center gap-2">✓ Document version archive with e-signatures</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="lg:col-span-6 reveal delay-100">
          <div class="rounded-card-lg border border-line bg-white p-3 shadow-elevated">
            <Image
              src={clientPortalImg}
              alt="Brift Client Portal showing feedback history and payment submission"
              class="w-full h-auto rounded-card object-cover"
              format="webp"
            />
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Audit Log Section -->
  <section class="py-16 sm:py-24 bg-white border-b border-line">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-12 gap-12 items-center">
        <div class="lg:col-span-6 lg:order-2 space-y-6 reveal">
          <span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-blue bg-blue-soft px-3 py-1 rounded-full">
            IMMUTABLE AUDIT TRAIL
          </span>
          <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-ink">
            Deleted isn't erased
          </h2>
          <p class="text-base text-muted leading-relaxed">
            In construction accounting, accidental deletions or intentional ledger tampering can create financial chaos. In Brift:
          </p>
          <div class="space-y-3 text-sm text-ink-2">
            <div class="rounded-xl border border-line bg-bg p-4 space-y-1">
              <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-ink">Reversing Entries</h3>
              <p class="text-xs text-muted leading-relaxed">Removing a verified bill posts an automated offsetting reversing entry, ensuring totals and balance history stay mathematically consistent.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="rounded-xl border border-line bg-bg p-4 space-y-1">
              <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-ink">Device & Author Logging</h3>
              <p class="text-xs text-muted leading-relaxed">Every action records exact author, time, IP address, and device footprint for complete peace of mind.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="lg:col-span-6 lg:order-1 reveal delay-100">
          <div class="rounded-card-lg border border-line bg-white p-3 shadow-elevated">
            <Image
              src={auditLogImg}
              alt="Brift Daily Activity Log showing admin verified actions and device timestamps"
              class="w-full h-auto rounded-card object-cover"
              format="webp"
            />
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CtaBanner />
</Layout>
